    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d96">

                <pb facs="0230" n="136" sameAs="frus:frus1930v03/pg136"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.5241/178</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Dawes</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-01-26">January 26, 1931</date>.<lb/>[Received February
                        4.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1594</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to refer to my despatch
                    No. 1297 of October 17, 1930,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d96-f1"/> regarding the
                    British Colonies and Protectorates which have not adhered to the Convention
                    concluded between the United States and Great Britain on March 2, 1899, relative
                    to the disposal of real and personal property in the respective countries, and
                    to enclose a copy, in triplicate, of a note which I have just received in reply
                    to my note addressed to the Foreign Office on October 17, 1930.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d96-f2"/></p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>(For the Ambassador)<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ray
                            Atherton</hi></signed><lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Counselor of
                        Embassy</hi></closer>


                <xi:include href="d96-a1.xml" xpointer="d96-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
